WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.222
At TREC UserSim 2026, we played a researcher looking
for datasets.

00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:07.982
The track organizers provided the search assistant.

00:00:08.402 --> 00:00:13.053
In Task 1, we predicted one researcher reply from a
supplied conversation.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:18.426
In Task 2, we exchanged messages with the assistant
and decided when to stop.

00:00:18.846 --> 00:00:23.539
Both model calls saw the researcher’s profile,
search goal, and dialogue so far.

00:00:23.739 --> 00:00:29.521
GPT-6 Luna drafted the next reply and decided
whether to continue in Task 2.

00:00:29.721 --> 00:00:35.182
A second call edited the wording. Task 2 kept the
draft’s decision to continue or stop.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:39.911
In one Task 2 search, the assistant suggested
WikiANN and WikiNeural.

00:00:40.111 --> 00:00:45.146
Our researcher asked about licenses, dataset splits,
and who had verified the labels.

00:00:45.346 --> 00:00:48.866
The editor kept that draft unchanged, and the search
continued.

00:00:49.286 --> 00:00:55.217
We submitted 62 predictions for Task 1 and processed
57 conversations for Task 2.

00:00:55.417 --> 00:00:59.150
Eight Task 2 conversations ended through
administrative closures.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:06.326
Preliminary mean human-likeness was 2.38 out of 4 in
Task 1 and 2.31 in Task 2.

00:01:06.746 --> 00:01:10.991
Our replies were longer on average than the human
replies in both tasks.

00:01:11.191 --> 00:01:17.378
The editor left 245 of 258 generated Task 2 drafts
word for word.

00:01:17.578 --> 00:01:20.223
The notebook paper has the scores and examples.
